\ Running this file raises import-conflict on `nip` and `dup`, so linting it reports both.

\\ Shadows the prelude's `nip`.
nip: ( x y -- y ) [ swap drop ] ;

\\ Shadows the native `dup`.
dup: ( x -- x x ) [ 0 ] ;

\\ Shadows the prelude's `tuck`, but claims the shadow deliberate.
tuck: override ( x y -- y x y ) [ swap over ] ;

\\ Its generated `name>>` is generic, and so is the prelude's, so the two are one extension point.
labelled: struct{ name } ;

\\ Takes no name from the base scope.
own-word: ( x -- x ) [ ] ;

\\ Redefines the prelude's const `fixnum`. `override` does not lift the const guard, so this reports.
fixnum: override ( -- x ) [ 1 ] ;
